From ecaa6235c5f0f26082c8a57f21bf97a8b24851df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Juan=20Manuel=20L=C3=B3pez=20Carrillo?=
 <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 12:01:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 098/143] pci: sunxi: reprogram the DMA-mapped MSI target on
 resume
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

sunxi_pcie_plat_resume() reprogrammed PCIE_MSI_ADDR_LO/HI with
ALIGN_DOWN(virt_to_phys(pp), SZ_4K) -- the physical address of the
driver's own sunxi_pcie_port struct in kernel RAM.  After resume any
endpoint MSI write lands inside that struct (silent memory
corruption) or faults the SMMU, depending on the IOMMU setup.

At probe sunxi_pcie_msi_init() instead DMA-maps &pp->msi_msg and
programs the resulting IOVA (pp->msi_data) into the controller; that
dma_map_single_attrs() mapping persists across suspend/resume as
long as the device stays bound, so on resume we only need to
reprogram the same IOVA into config space -- no remap needed.

Also switch the gate from the compile-time IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PCI_MSI)
to the runtime pci_msi_enabled(), matching the probe path: when MSI
is disabled at runtime the probe path leaves the registers alone, so
resume must too, or the controller would point at an MSI target that
nothing ever set up.

Signed-off-by: Juan Manuel López Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c b/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
index dc73eb861..c273828d0 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pcie-sunxi/pcie-sunxi-plat.c
@@ -1186,10 +1186,24 @@ static int sunxi_pcie_plat_resume(struct device *dev)
 		sunxi_pcie_plat_ltssm_disable(pci);
 		sunxi_pcie_host_setup_rc(pp);
 
-		if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PCI_MSI) && !pp->has_its) {
-			phys_addr_t pa = ALIGN_DOWN(virt_to_phys(pp), SZ_4K);
-			sunxi_pcie_host_wr_own_conf(pp, PCIE_MSI_ADDR_LO, 4, lower_32_bits(pa));
-			sunxi_pcie_host_wr_own_conf(pp, PCIE_MSI_ADDR_HI, 4, upper_32_bits(pa));
+		if (pci_msi_enabled() && !pp->has_its) {
+			/*
+			 * Reprogram the MSI target address that suspend cleared
+			 * from the controller's config space.  Use the same IOVA
+			 * that was DMA-mapped in sunxi_pcie_msi_init() at probe:
+			 * the dma_map_single_attrs() mapping is persistent across
+			 * suspend/resume as long as the device stays bound, so
+			 * pp->msi_data is still valid.  Programming
+			 * virt_to_phys(pp) here (a kernel-RAM address) would
+			 * route endpoint MSI writes into the driver's own
+			 * struct (or fault the SMMU) and corrupt memory.
+			 */
+			u64 msi_target = (u64)pp->msi_data;
+
+			sunxi_pcie_host_wr_own_conf(pp, PCIE_MSI_ADDR_LO, 4,
+						    lower_32_bits(msi_target));
+			sunxi_pcie_host_wr_own_conf(pp, PCIE_MSI_ADDR_HI, 4,
+						    upper_32_bits(msi_target));
 		}
 
 		sunxi_pcie_host_establish_link(pci);
-- 
